On Thursday 06 May 2004 17:41 Thomas Wesley Hinton
(wesleyREMOVETHIS@worldonline.dk) wrote:

> I have attempted of saccing some orks to my god, I'm a lawful valk. I
> just get the message "nothing happends", and I still have the corpse
> in my inv.
> 
> Is the sac to small, or is my god pissed at me for playin "lawful
> stupid" (I just killed everything that moved in minetown, but I
> figured I could just chuck gems at a white unicorn, and eat some
> floating eye and avoid all negative consequences).

No, you've been carrying them around too long, gods want really fresh
corpses. Killing monsters on the altar is the best way to sacrifice
heavy things; if you sacrifice orcs, which aren't all that heavy, it's
wise to do it close to the altar and carry one at a time so you don't
get stressed.

Also, if you pick up a fresh corpse when you're already carrying an old
corpse, the age gets averaged so they may both be too old. The same
goes for piling corpses on an altar.

And watch out for orc zombies: they may leave orc corpses, but they're
already too old to sacrifice when you destroy them.

Your god won't get angry if you sacrifice something that's too old, by
the way; only if you sacrifice something really inappropriate that
isn't too old.

   Raisse, killed by a hill orc

